hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1586","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Qaisi told us, Abu Amir told us, and Muhammad bin Muammar also told us, Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Zarbi, a client of Al Al-Muhallab said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “God has given me three qualities.” A man from his companions: What are these qualities, O Messenger of God? He said: “He gave me prayer in the rows, and he gave me the greeting. It is the greeting of the people of Paradise, and he gave me insurance, and he did not give it to any of the prophets.” Before, unless God gave it to Aaron, Moses would pray and Aaron would believe.”"
